		{"id":"legend_node","type":"text","text":"### 🎨 Status & Color Legend\n- **Default (No Color)**: To Learn\n- **Yellow (Color 3)**: In Progress\n- **Orange (Color 2)**: Review/Apply\n- **Green (Color 4)**: Mastered","x":-200,"y":-720,"width":420,"height":180},
		{"id":"interview_banner","type":"text","text":"# 🔴 SME Level 2 Technical Round\n**Role:** Senior Cloud DevOps Engineer\n**Target:** SME Level 2 Technical Interview\n**Product:** RapidResponse Enterprise SaaS\n**Key Focus:** Terraform, Python, GHA vs Argo, CI/CD, Bots","x":260,"y":-720,"width":480,"height":180,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"guide_resume","type":"text","text":"### [[1. Resume-Mapped Interview Answers|1. Resume-Mapped Answers]]\n\n🎯 **Your Personal Pitch & 7 ADP/Genxlead Stories**\n*Airport concourses, smart kitchen, ATC radar...*","x":-970,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_strategy","type":"text","text":"### [[2. Hiring Manager Prep & Strategy|2. HM Prep & Strategy]]\n\n🧠 **HM Mindset, AWS-to-GCP Bridge & Questions**\n*Leadership, ADRs, blameless culture, 4 smart questions*","x":-550,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_concepts","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide|3. Concepts & Analogies Guide]]\n\n🔬 **11 Technical Deep Dives with Full Analogies**\n*Capsule, ARC, ArgoCD, WIF, Vault, Shared VPC, Ansible*","x":-130,"y":-430,"width":420,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_jd","type":"text","text":"### [[4. Job Description & Role Overview|4. Job Description & Overview]]\n\n📋 **Target Role Profile & Requirements**\n*RapidResponse context & skill requirements checklist*","x":330,"y":-430,"width":370,"height":190,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_farm","type":"text","text":"### 1. Istio Farm-Based Routing\n**Analogy:** ✈️ Airport Terminal Concourses\n- **Impact:** Eliminated noisy neighbors on EKS; protected 99.99% SLAs\n- **Tech:** Split Gateways, VirtualService, DestinationRule, Sidecar scoping\n- **Maps to:** Capsule Multi-Tenancy on GKE","x":-1010,"y":-80,"width":500,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_keda","type":"text","text":"### 2. KEDA Event-Driven Scaling\n**Analogy:** 🍳 Smart Kitchen: Instant Induction Burners\n- **Impact:** 80% compute cost cut; scaled 0 to 200+ nodes on demand\n- **Tech:** Queue-depth autoscaling, Scale-to-Zero, Spot node pools\n- **Maps to:** Actions Runner Controller (ARC) on GKE","x":-1010,"y":160,"width":500,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_arc","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#2-actions-runner-controller-arc-on-gke|1. ARC on GKE (CI/CD Compute)]]\n**Analogy:** 🚗 Ephemeral Drone Fleet vs. Idling Limousines\n- **Problem:** Static VM runners sit idle 24/7 and share dirty state/tokens\n- **Solution:** Ephemeral runner pods scale 0-to-200 on Spot nodes; self-destruct after 1 job\n- **Interview Pitch:** Scale-to-Zero FinOps + private VPC access without dirty caches.","x":230,"y":-120,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_argocd","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#3-argo-cd--gitops-with-applicationsets|2. Argo CD & ApplicationSets]]\n**Analogy:** 🚢 Autopilot Cargo Vessel vs. Delivery Trucks\n- **Problem:** Push CI requires cluster-admin keys; manual kubectl drift is undetected\n- **Solution:** Pull-based GitOps; selfHeal auto-reverts drift; AppSets stamp out multi-cluster apps\n- **Interview Pitch:** Certified Argo Project Associate (CAPA); Git is single source of truth.","x":230,"y":160,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_capsule","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#1-capsule-kubernetes-multi-tenancy-operator|1. Capsule (K8s Multi-Tenancy)]]\n**Analogy:** 🏢 High-Rise: Leased Floors vs. Single Rooms\n- **Problem:** Cluster sprawl (40+ GKE clusters) vs. Ticket-ops for namespaces\n- **Solution:** Tenant CRD, aggregate CPU/RAM quotas, regex Ingress & StorageClass whitelist\n- **Interview Pitch:** Pairs with Istio farm routing for complete multi-tenant governance.","x":-380,"y":-40,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_wif","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#6-gcp-workload-identity-federation-wif-vs-aws-irsa|3. Workload Identity Federation (WIF)]]\n**Analogy:** 🪪 15-Minute Biometric Temp Badges vs. Permanent Brass Keys\n- **Problem:** Static service account JSON keys leak in Git/Docker images\n- **Solution:** GCP WIF (IRSA counterpart): GKE Metadata server exchanges K8s JWT for temp Google tokens\n- **Interview Pitch:** Zero downloadable keys policy; least-privilege pod identity.","x":-380,"y":700,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_supplychain","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#8-container-supply-chain-security-trivy-sbom-cosign|4. Supply Chain Security (Trivy + Cosign)]]\n**Analogy:** 🔍 Airport Customs X-Ray & Diplomatic Wax Seal\n- **Problem:** Vulnerable base images & registry image tampering in production\n- **Solution:** Trivy blocks Critical CVEs in CI; Syft generates SBOM; Cosign signs image; GKE admission verifies\n- **Interview Pitch:** Shift-left security in pipeline + zero-trust gate at cluster admission.","x":-380,"y":1060,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_windows","type":"text","text":"### 7. Windows Modernization to K8s\n**Analogy:** 🖨️ Upgrading Hand-Cranked to Cloud Digital Presses\n- **Impact:** 100% manual effort eliminated; handled 80% more jobs at peak\n- **Tech:** Migrated legacy Windows testing to AWS EKS with Fargate\n- **Maps to:** Ansible WinRM Windows Server Automation","x":-1010,"y":1400,"width":500,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_finops","type":"text","text":"### 6. Platform FinOps & Log Reduction\n**Analogy:** 📦 Tetris Packing Robot & Postal Shredder\n- **Impact:** Just-in-time compute consolidation; slashed Datadog/Splunk ingestion\n- **Tech:** Karpenter + Shared Ingress + Cribl pipeline data reduction\n- **Maps to:** Cloud Usage & Cost Optimization initiatives","x":-1010,"y":1140,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_crossplane","type":"text","text":"### 5. Multi-Account Analytics Control Plane\n**Analogy:** 🛰️ Central Satellite Dish / Federated Telescope\n- **Impact:** Federated SQL across 5 AWS accounts; onboarding 3 days → 30 mins\n- **Tech:** Crossplane K8s control plane + Redash + Athena federation\n- **Maps to:** Multi-Project GCP Governance & Workload Identity","x":-1010,"y":860,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_bots","type":"text","text":"### 4. Self-Service Infra Bots\n**Analogy:** 🏧 Automated Bank Smart ATMs\n- **Impact:** Cut sandbox provisioning lead time from 2 days to <10 mins\n- **Tech:** Python & Go automation bots with compliance guardrails\n- **Maps to:** Developer Productivity & Platform Golden Paths","x":-1010,"y":620,"width":500,"height":240,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"story_golang","type":"text","text":"### 3. Golang Release Observability\n**Analogy:** 📡 Air Traffic Control Live Radar\n- **Impact:** Saved 8 man-hours of manual monitoring per release\n- **Tech:** High-throughput logging engine & live dashboard in Go\n- **Maps to:** Go/Python Platform Tooling & Self-Service","x":-1010,"y":390,"width":500,"height":230,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_terraform_ansible","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#10-terraform-layered-architecture--blast-radius-management|3. Layered Terraform & Ansible WinRM]]\n**Analogy:** 🧱 Battleship Bulkheads & Universal Factory Foreman\n- **Problem:** Monolithic tfstate blast radius; manual Windows RDP pets and drift\n- **Solution:** Layered state files (IAM → VPC → Platform → Apps); Ansible over HTTPS WinRM for Windows\n- **Interview Pitch:** Mathematical isolation of blast radius; automated Windows baseline hardening.","x":230,"y":1250,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_psc","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#5-private-service-connect-psc-vs-aws-privatelink|2. Private Service Connect (PSC)]]\n**Analogy:** 🚪 Secret VIP Hotel Tunnel (No Street Exposure)\n- **Problem:** VPC Peering causes CIDR overlap crashes if both sides use 10.0.0.0/16\n- **Solution:** Unidirectional private service forwarding rule; 100% immune to IP collisions\n- **Interview Pitch:** Expose SaaS platform APIs privately without public IPs or routing table merges.","x":230,"y":970,"width":500,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_sharedvpc","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#4-gcp-shared-vpc-vs-aws-transit-gateway--ram|1. GCP Shared VPC vs. AWS TGW]]\n**Analogy:** 🛣️ Global National Highway vs. Regional Toll Bridges\n- **Problem:** AWS VPCs are regional silos requiring expensive Transit Gateway hops\n- **Solution:** GCP Shared VPC is global; Host Project shares subnets directly to GKE with $0 transit fees\n- **Interview Pitch:** 1:1 mapping: centralized IPAM, no CIDR collision, zero network hop latency.","x":230,"y":700,"width":500,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"node_sre","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#11-production-incident-triage-sre--blameless-post-mortems|3. SRE Incident Triage & RCA]]\n**Analogy:** 🚒 ER Trauma Team: Stop the Bleeding First\n- **Problem:** Chaos and blame during Sev-1 outages; fixing symptoms instead of systems\n- **Solution:** Incident Commander vs Technical Primaries; MTTR rollback first, 5-Whys blameless RCA second\n- **Interview Pitch:** Turn outages into automated policy-as-code guardrails.","x":230,"y":430,"width":500,"height":270,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f2e6c99c8b111f97","x":1168,"y":-684,"width":392,"height":564,"type":"text","text":"# 🔴  Genxlead\n\nEc2 Automation\nCDN Hosting.\nAnsible Scripts\nsnowflake\n\n\n\n"},
		{"id":"d018b923858d30b4","x":1580,"y":-684,"width":360,"height":564,"type":"text","text":"# 🔴  ADP\n\n\nRelease Engineer\nRelease Dashboard\nREdash\nSelenium Grid\nIstio Farm based\nBotops Works\nOS Redemition\n"},
		{"id":"9854e763ed67cea2","x":1980,"y":-684,"width":340,"height":524,"type":"text","text":"# 🔴  TOOLS\n\nTerraform\nArgoworkflow\nPython\nETL BASH & python"},
		{"id":"node_vault","type":"text","text":"### [[3. Core Concepts & Analogies Guide#7-hashicorp-vault-on-kubernetes-dynamic-secrets--sidecars|2. HashiCorp Vault on K8s]]\n**Analogy:** ⏳ Mission Impossible Self-Destructing Passcodes\n- **Problem:** Plaintext base64 secrets in etcd & static permanent DB passwords\n- **Solution:** Vault Agent Injector sidecar into in-memory tmpfs volume; dynamic leased DB credentials\n- **Interview Pitch:** Eliminates static credentials; secrets never touch physical disk.","x":-380,"y":305,"width":500,"height":295,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_python","type":"text","text":"### [[5. Python ETL & Scripting Mastery|5. Python ETL & Scripting]]\n\n🐍 **Farm-to-Table Juice Factory Analogy**\n*Defensive parsing, generators, defaultdict & ETL script*","x":730,"y":-430,"width":390,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_terraform","type":"text","text":"### [[8. Terraform Basics & Senior Q&A Mastery|8. Terraform Basics & Q&A]]\n\n🏗️ **Architect Blueprint & Land Registry Analogy**\n*State locking, for_each vs count, Atlantis GitOps & Q&A*","x":1140,"y":-430,"width":400,"height":120,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"guide_sme","type":"text","text":"### [[6. SME Level 2 Technical Round Mastery|6. SME Level 2 Technical Mastery]]\n\n🎯 **5 Core Pillars for Technical Round**\n*Terraform, Python, GHA vs Argo, CI/CD Process & Bots*","x":1560,"y":-430,"width":420,"height":190,"color":"4"}
